.hermes\desktop-attachments\The Dialectical Engine_ Architectural Blueprint for a Multi-Provider Epistemic AI System-2.md:152:- **Community-Notes bridging (swarm).** A swarm contribution gains weight only when raters/models that *usually disagree* both endorse it. Implement the matrix-factorization bridging model: rating ≈ μ + i_user + i_note + f_user·f_note; the note intercept i_note (after factoring out the polarity dot-product f_user·f_note) is the bridged quality score.  High i_note = broadly helpful across polarities. WHY: prevents a single partisan/model-family bloc from upvoting its own contributions. 
