.hermes\plans\2026-07-24-graph-harness-migration-plan-v1.md:148:- **D5 (2026-07-24): THE ONE-PROMPT MACHINE.** Inherited from the full protocol and cemented as spine law: exactly one V prompt starts a mission (H0). Thereafter only three V-facing surfaces exist: **(a)** design questions/steering, emitted ONLY by the REQUIREMENTS (H0) and ARCHITECTURE (planning diamond C2/H2/G3/H3/C4) nodes, during design; **(b)** IMPORTANT-OPERATION decisions (database deletion, data manipulation, security/auth, provider spend, destructive git/filesystem, architecture/scope expansion, reconstructed evidence, waiver) from any node, exclusively via the batched `V DECISIONS PACKET`; **(c)** final acceptance (H9). V never relays prompts or output; no other node addresses V; Claude-Router intercepts violations. Installed by Task 3.11(l); enforced as default operation by Task 6.3. All other rulings and decisions in this register remain unchanged.
